09b2"} {"question" "q-110449" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-110449" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-110760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\n- $A={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:x-4y=1}$\n- $B={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:x=-2y}$\n- $C={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}<0}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-110760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's analyze each subset.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. For instance, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the equation $x-4y=1$ since $0-4\\cdot 0=0\\ne 1.$\n\n- The set $B$ is a subspace. It represents a plane, and a plane is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $x=-2y$ since $0=-2\\cdot 0.$ So $0$ lies in $B.$\n\n- The set $C$ is not a subspace. No point in ${R}^{3}$ satisfies the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}<0.$ Hence, $C=∅.$ The empty set is not a subspace since it does not contain the zero vector.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-110760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80f8cf5dcadec8f80f7d327e9e5b890f1e02b0f3bbca61f35f7c8d4db8d0c764"} {"question" "q-110760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-110760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-110760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-35599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{2}?$\n\n- $A={⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 0}$\n- $B={⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:x=\\frac{1}{2}y+2}$\n- $C={0}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-35599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is a subspace. There is only one vector in ${R}^{2}$ that satisfies the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 0,$ namely, the zero vector $0=⟨0,0⟩.$ So, $A={0}$, which is a special subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The set $B$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the equation $x=\\frac{1}{2}y+2$ since $0\\ne \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0+2.$\n\n- The set $C$ is a subspace. This subset has only one element, the zero vector $0=⟨0,0⟩,$ which is a special subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-35599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80f8cf5dcadec8f80f7d327e9e5b890f1e02b0f3bbca61f35f7c8d4db8d0c764"} {"question" "q-35599" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-35599" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-35599" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-110611" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\n- $A={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:xyz=1}$\n- $B={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:x+y-z=0}$\n- $C={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:y=-1}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-110611" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the condition $xyz=1$ since $0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0\\ne 1.$\n\n- The set $B$ is a subspace. It represents a plane, and a plane is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $x+y-z=0$ since $0+0-0=0.$ So $0$ lies in $B.$\n\n- The set $C$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the condition $y=-1$ since $0\\ne -1.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-110611" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80f8cf5dcadec8f80f7d327e9e5b890f1e02b0f3bbca61f35f7c8d4db8d0c764"} {"question" "q-110611" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-110611" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-110611" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-74218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\n- $A={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1}$\n- $B={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:xyz=0}$\n- $C={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:y=-1}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-74218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the condition ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1$ since ${0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}\\ne 1.$\n\n- The set $B$ is not a subspace because it is not closed under vector addition. Indeed, both $a=⟨1,0,1⟩$ and $b=⟨0,1,1⟩$ belong to $B$ but \n\n$$\na+b=⟨1,0,1⟩+⟨0,1,1⟩=⟨1,1,2⟩\n$$\n\n \ndoes not satisfy the condition $xyz=0$ since $1\\cdot 1\\cdot 2\\ne 0.$\n\n- The set $C$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the condition $y=-1$ since $0\\ne -1.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-74218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80f8cf5dcadec8f80f7d327e9e5b890f1e02b0f3bbca61f35f7c8d4db8d0c764"} {"question" "q-74218" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-74218" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-74218" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "None"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-74217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\n- $A={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:1-x-y=0}$\n- $B={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le 1}$\n- $C={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:2x+3y-z=0}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-74217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the equation $1-x-y=0$ since $1-0-0\\ne 0.$\n\n- The set $B$ is not a subspace. Indeed, the vector $u=⟨1,0,0⟩$ is in $B$, but $2u=⟨2,0,0⟩$ is not in $B$, since ${2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}≰1.$ So, $B$ is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- The set $C$ is a subspace. It represents a plane, and a plane is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $2x+3y-z=0$ since $2\\cdot 0+3\\cdot 0-0=0.$ So $0$ lies in $C.$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/state.json" "file_sha256" "d69d55414fec1fbdfb074ecc648f84bbc1400ac826d783e5b7649907ee3d09b2"} {"question" "q-74217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "ca